  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Green chemistry in day-to-day life is in the use of:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "fSQuS",
      "text": "Chlorine for bleaching of paper",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NGBGK",
      "text": "Large amount of water alone for washing clothes",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d7gJ3",
      "text": "Tetrachloroethene for laundry",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ETtVN",
      "text": "Liquified <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> for dry cleaning of clothes",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Chlorine gas was used earlier for bleaching paper. These days, hydrogen peroxide <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is used with suitable catalyst.</p><p>Tetrachloroethene <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>CCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;was earlier used as solvent for dry cleaning. The compound contaminates the ground water and is also a suspected carcinogen. Replacement of halogenated solvent by liquid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> will result in less harm to groundwater. Hence, given statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is correct.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
